# pnpm's default (isolated) layout: every dependency under node_modules/.pnpm, symlinked into the
# workspace that names it. Nothing here needs a hoisted one.

# The published Beacon packages (@beaconsgg/*) come from the public npm registry: the client side of
# the platform the console is written over, the plugin contract's three peers, and the build, test,
# lint and format presets.
# An install needs no token. A token is needed only to publish, and it never goes in this file:
# pnpm drops this whole file when a ${VAR} in it is unset. The release workflow writes it to the
# runner's user config from the NPM_TOKEN repository secret.
# No game's scope is mapped here: the repository installs no game plugin. A deployment that adds one
# (apps/admin/scripts/add-plugins.mjs) maps the plugin's scope in its own user config, beside the
# token, and a scope it does not map is asked of npmjs.
